'''Grup Pastel, S.A.''' ({{lang|ca|Grup Pastel}}; "Pastel Group") is a Balboan hospitality and tourism company and the country's largest hotel and holiday package operator. Headquartered in the [[Districte Financer (Original, Sant Cristòfor)|Districte Financer]] of [[Sant Cristòfor]], the company operates a portfolio of hotels, resorts, and holiday properties across the Balboan isthmus, and provides package holidays, tour operations, and cruise excursions to domestic and international visitors. It is listed on the [[Bolsa de Sant Cristòfor]] under the ticker GPT.

Grup Pastel was founded in 1978, shortly after reunification, to capitalise on the anticipated growth of Balboan tourism as the country reintegrated Sant Cristòfor and the canal corridor into the national economy. The company's name — "pastel" meaning "cake" or "pastry" in Balboan — was chosen to evoke the colourful, confection-like appearance of the traditional Balboan coastal architecture, and the company's branding has consistently used the pastel colour palette associated with the Estret corridor's waterfront buildings.

The company is the dominant player in the Balboan hospitality sector, operating 42 properties across the isthmus, from the beach resorts of the Costa Nord to the mountain lodges of the Tramuntana highlands.

== History ==

=== Founding (1978) ===

Grup Pastel was founded in 1978 by [[Rosa Masdeu i Vidal]], a Portnou hotelier, and [[Tân Hô-lêng]], a Zong-Balboan businesswoman whose family had operated boarding houses in the Sant Cristòfor port district during the Zong Balboa period. The two women identified an opportunity in the post-reunification tourism market: the return of Sant Cristòfor and the canal corridor to Balboan sovereignty had opened the Estret coastline — with its beaches, its historic port cities, and its proximity to the canal — to domestic and international tourism for the first time in over seventy years.

The existing hotel infrastructure in the Estret corridor was dilapidated. The Zong Balboa period had produced a modest hospitality sector serving the canal trade and the Zong military, but the siege of the Great Adonian War and the subsequent mandate period had left the properties in poor condition. The interior, meanwhile, had a small network of planter-era guesthouses and government rest houses that were inadequate for the anticipated tourism demand.

Masdeu i Vidal and Tân Hô-lêng raised capital from the Portnou business community and the Zong-Balboan merchant families, and acquired three properties in their first year: the Hotel Marítim in Portnou, a former Zong-era boarding house on the waterfront; the Hotel Estret in Sant Cristòfor, a mandate-era government guesthouse; and the Hotel Tramuntana in the highlands, a former planter retreat. The three properties were renovated and reopened under the Grup Pastel brand in 1979.

=== Expansion (1978–2000) ===

The Balboan tourism sector grew rapidly in the 1980s and 1990s, driven by the recovery of the canal corridor, the expansion of international air connections, and the country's growing reputation as a tropical destination with a unique cultural heritage. Grup Pastel expanded its portfolio aggressively, acquiring existing properties and developing new ones along the Estret coastline and in the interior highlands.

The company's strategy was to offer a vertically integrated tourism experience: the customer could book a package holiday through Grup Pastel's tour operation, stay in a Grup Pastel hotel, eat at a Grup Pastel restaurant, and take a Grup Pastel excursion to the canal or the interior. The vertical integration allowed the company to capture the full value chain of the tourist's spending, and it provided a consistent brand experience that differentiated Grup Pastel from the smaller, independent operators.

The company was listed on the [[Bolsa de Sant Cristòfor]] in 1992, raising capital that was used to fund the development of the Costa Nord resort complex — a 400-room beachfront resort on the northern Aethiopian coast that became the company's flagship property. The [[Fons d'Inversió Directa de Balboa]] acquired a 5 per cent stake at the time of the listing.

The [[Balboa real-estate asset crisis]] and the [[1994 Balboa spot recession]] reduced tourist arrivals temporarily, but the company's diversified portfolio — which included budget properties that benefited from the shift toward domestic tourism during the downturn — allowed it to weather the contraction. The company emerged from the recession in a stronger competitive position, as several smaller operators had collapsed.

=== Modern era (2000–present) ===

The 2000s and 2010s saw Grup Pastel expand into the international market, establishing tour operations that brought visitors from Volisania, Zong, and Sinchew to the Balboan isthmus. The company also developed a cruise excursion programme, partnering with the canal cruise operators to offer shore-based packages for passengers transiting the canal.

The [[Adonian pandemic]] of 2020 was the most severe crisis in the company's history. The collapse of international travel reduced occupancy rates across the portfolio to single digits, and the company was forced to close most of its properties and furlough the majority of its workforce. The company accessed government support programmes and negotiated rent deferrals with its property landlords, and it survived the pandemic by focusing on domestic tourism — which recovered faster than international travel — and by offering long-stay packages for remote workers.

The pandemic also produced a significant change in the company's ownership structure. The collapse in the share price — which fell from $42 in February 2020 to $14 in November 2020 — attracted the attention of two international investors. In 2022, [[Grup Extraviatjar]], the Volisanian travel conglomerate, acquired a 10 per cent stake, citing the long-term recovery potential of the Balboan tourism sector and the strategic value of Grup Pastel's property portfolio. In the same year, [[BLEC]] (Varkan: ბლეჩ), the Varkan private investment management firm controlled by the Bajusz–Latso family, acquired an 8 per cent stake. The investments, which were made at a significant discount to the pre-pandemic share price, provided Grup Pastel with capital that was used to refurbish properties and fund the post-pandemic recovery.

The recovery was rapid: by 2023, occupancy rates had returned to pre-pandemic levels, and the company's revenue exceeded its 2019 figures. The post-pandemic period has been characterised by a shift toward higher-end properties and experiential tourism, as the company has sought to increase its average revenue per available room.

By 2026, Grup Pastel employed approximately 9,400 people and operated 42 properties across the isthmus.

== Operations ==

Grup Pastel operates across five principal business lines:

* '''Hotels and resorts''': The company's core business, operating 42 properties across four segments — luxury (5 properties), premium (12), mid-range (18), and budget (7). The properties are concentrated in the Estret corridor (22), the Costa Nord (10), and the interior highlands (10).
* '''Package holidays''': The company's tour operation, offering all-inclusive holiday packages that combine accommodation, flights, transfers, and excursions. The package holiday division is the primary channel through which international visitors book Grup Pastel properties.
* '''Tour operations''': Guided excursions to the canal, the interior highlands, the Birú cultural sites, and the wildlife reserves of Nurra. The tour operations division also operates the company's cruise excursion programme.
* '''Cruise excursions''': Shore-based packages for passengers transiting the Balboa Canal on cruise ships, including city tours of Sant Cristòfor, canal-side dining, and highland day trips.
* '''Food and beverage''': The company operates restaurants, bars, and catering services across its hotel portfolio, including several standalone restaurants in Sant Cristòfor and Portnou.

The company's headquarters are at 24 Passeig Marítim, in the Districte Financer of Sant Cristòfor, and it maintains regional offices in Portnou, Sant Bart, and Ampuria.

